From fa9ccb7c5cc4e11c70000879201613ec7c34a3fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 21:31:26 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 212/348] Part: 2D export with hidden lines removed (SVG,
 polygons JSON, PPTX)

  FreeCADCmd model.step --view iso --export-svg v.svg --export-polygons v.json
             --export-pptx v.pptx

Part.projectVisible(objects, view) projects orthographically and removes
hidden parts exactly (no pixels involved), for redrawing a model as shapes:

- faces: every visible region of each face as polygons with holes, in model
  units (x right, y up), with depth, a simple light shade and colour, sorted
  far to near.  Planar faces are handled as a whole, curved faces per
  triangle and merged again; meshes by smooth patches.  The visible part of
  a face is its projection minus the parts of other faces that are nearer
  there (the depth of planar pieces is linear, so "nearer" is a half plane
  clipped with Clipper2) - interpenetrating parts are cut correctly.
- edges: sharp, smooth (tangent) and silhouette edges, clipped exactly
  against the nearer faces; edges lying on the outline of a nearer face are
  dropped, so no line is drawn twice.

PartViews writes SVG (filled faces plus edges), JSON and, without
python-pptx, a minimal PowerPoint file with one slide: each visible face
region a freeform shape (editable, recolourable), edges as lines.  Checked
by reading it back with python-pptx; not yet opened in PowerPoint itself.

300 parts: projection 2.0 s, SVG 2.0 s.  Tests check exact visible areas
and edge lengths (a box partly hidden behind another), iso box (3 faces,
9 edges) and cylinder silhouettes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
